<title>PANAMA: Panama qualifies Cable &amp; Wireless for phone sale.</title>
<headline>Panama qualifies Cable &amp; Wireless for phone sale.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama qualified British telecommunications company Cable and Wireless Plc to take part in the sale of state telephone utility National Telecommunications Institute (INTEL), a government spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;Cable &amp; Wireless was pre-qualified recently. Now they and GTE are reviewing documents about INTEL,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Panama qualified GTE Corp of the United States earlier this year.</p>
<p>Panama extended the pre-qualification process to allow more companies to take part in the INTEL sale after key bidder SBC Communications Inc pulled out.</p>
<p>INTEL's value is estimated at $2 billion with assets of $450 million.</p>
<p>-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739</p>
